quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  19,65,"(He is) the Lord of the heavens, the earth and whatever is between them. So worship Him (alone) and be steadfast in His worship. Do you know anyone who could be His namesake?’"
  19,66,"Man says: ‘What? Once I am dead, shall I truly be brought out alive?’"
  19,67,Does human being not remember that We had created him before when he was nothing?
  19,68,"So, by your Lord, We shall surely gather them and the devils. Then, We shall surely cause them to be present around Hell (scrambling) on their knees."
  19,69,"Then, from every group, We shall surely drag out whichever of them was the most rebellious against the Most-Compassionate (Lord)."
  19,70,"Again, surely, We know best those most deserving to be thrown into Hell."
  19,71,"And there is none of you but will pass over it*. (This is) a decree of your Lord, certainly determined."
  19,72,"Then We will deliver those who are God-conscious and leave the wrongdoers in it, falling on their knees."
  19,73,"When Our clear revelations are recited to them, the disbelievers say to the believers: ‘Which of the two groups (i.e. yours or ours) is superior in station and better in company.’"
  19,74,And how many a generation have We destroyed before them who were superior in worldly riches and outward glitter!
  19,75,"Say: ‘Whoever remains upon misguidance, the Most-Compassionate (Lord) shall prolong his life until they see what they have been warned about—either punishment (in this life) or the Hour (of the judgement). Then they will come to know who was in a bad position and (who was) weaker as an army."
  19,76,And Allah increases in guidance those who are rightly guided. And the lasting deeds of righteousness are better with your Lord in reward and better in return.
